---Features and available amenities in the guest unit.
---@class gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeatures
---@field suiteException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesSuiteExceptionEnum|string Suite exception.
---@field suite? boolean Suite. A guestroom category that implies both a bedroom area and a separate living area. There may or may not be full walls and doors separating the two areas, but regardless, they are very distinct. Does not mean a couch or chair in a bedroom.
---@field bungalowOrVillaException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesBungalowOrVillaExceptionEnum|string Bungalow or villa exception.
---@field bungalowOrVilla? boolean Bungalow or villa. An independent structure that is part of a hotel or resort that is rented to one party for a vacation stay. The hotel or resort may be completely comprised of bungalows or villas, or they may be one of several guestroom options. Guests in the bungalows or villas most often have the same, if not more, amenities and services offered to guests in other guestroom types.
---@field connectingUnitAvailable? boolean Connecting unit available. A guestroom type that features access to an adjacent guestroom for the purpose of booking both rooms. Most often used by families who need more than one room to accommodate the number of people in their group.
---@field maxChildOccupantsCountException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesMaxChildOccupantsCountExceptionEnum|string Max child occupants count exception.
---@field executiveFloor? boolean Executive floor. A floor of the hotel where the guestrooms are only bookable by members of the hotel's frequent guest membership program. Benefits of this room class include access to a designated lounge which may or may not feature free breakfast, cocktails or other perks specific to members of the program.
---@field executiveFloorException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesExecutiveFloorExceptionEnum|string Executive floor exception.
---@field connectingUnitAvailableException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesConnectingUnitAvailableExceptionEnum|string Connecting unit available exception.
---@field privateHomeException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesPrivateHomeExceptionEnum|string Private home exception.
---@field tierException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesTierExceptionEnum|string Tier exception.
---@field maxOccupantsCount? number Max occupants count. The total number of guests allowed to stay overnight in the guestroom.
---@field maxAdultOccupantsCount? number Max adult occupants count. The total number of adult guests allowed to stay overnight in the guestroom.
---@field tier? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesTierEnum|string Tier. Classification of the unit based on available features/amenities. A non-standard tier is only permitted if at least one other unit type falls under the standard tier.
---@field maxOccupantsCountException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesMaxOccupantsCountExceptionEnum|string Max occupants count exception.
---@field maxChildOccupantsCount? number Max child occupants count. The total number of children allowed to stay overnight in the room.
---@field privateHome? boolean Private home. A privately owned home (house, townhouse, apartment, cabin, bungalow etc) that may or not serve as the owner's residence, but is rented out in its entirety or by the room(s) to paying guest(s) for vacation stays. Not for lease-based, long-term residency.
---@field totalLivingAreas? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.LivingArea Features available in the living areas in the guest unit.
---@field views? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.ViewsFromUnit Views available from the guest unit itself.
---@field maxAdultOccupantsCountException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesMaxAdultOccupantsCountExceptionEnum|string Max adult occupants count exception.

---@alias gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.GuestUnitFeaturesBungalowOrVillaExceptionEnum "EXCEPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"UNDER_CONSTRUCTION"|"DEPENDENT_ON_SEASON"|"DEPENDENT_ON_DAY_OF_WEEK"

