---@field minibarException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.LivingAreaEatingMinibarExceptionEnum|string Minibar exception.
---@field minibar? boolean Minibar. A small refrigerated cabinet in the guestroom containing bottles/cans of soft drinks, mini bottles of alcohol, and snacks. The items are most commonly available for a fee.
---@field coffeeMakerException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.LivingAreaEatingCoffeeMakerExceptionEnum|string Coffee maker exception.
---@field teaStationException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.LivingAreaEatingTeaStationExceptionEnum|string Tea station exception.
---@field teaStation? boolean Tea station. A small area with the supplies needed to heat water and make tea.
---@field refrigeratorException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.LivingAreaEatingRefrigeratorExceptionEnum|string Refrigerator exception.
---@field outdoorGrillException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.LivingAreaEatingOutdoorGrillExceptionEnum|string Outdoor grill exception.
---@field outdoorGrill? boolean Outdoor grill. Metal grates on which food is cooked over an open flame or electric heat source. Part of an outdoor apparatus that supports the grates. Also known as barbecue grill or barbecue.
---@field coffeeMaker? boolean Coffee maker. An electric appliance that brews coffee by heating and forcing water through ground coffee.
---@field sink? boolean Sink. A basin with a faucet attached to a water source and used for the purpose of washing and rinsing.
---@field microwave? boolean Microwave. An electric oven that quickly cooks and heats food by microwave energy. Smaller than a standing or wall mounted oven. Usually placed on a kitchen counter, a shelf or tabletop or mounted above a cooktop.
---@field kitchenAvailableException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.LivingAreaEatingKitchenAvailableExceptionEnum|string Kitchen available exception.
---@field cookware? boolean Cookware. Kitchen pots, pans and utensils used in connection with the preparation of food.
---@field dishwasher? boolean Dishwasher. A counter-height electrical cabinet containing racks for dirty dishware, cookware and cutlery, and a dispenser for soap built into the pull-down door. The cabinet is attached to the plumbing system to facilitate the automatic cleaning of its contents.
---@field stove? boolean Stove. A kitchen appliance powered by gas or electricity for the purpose of creating a flame or hot surface on which pots of food can be cooked. Also known as cooktop or hob.
---@field dishwasherException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.LivingAreaEatingDishwasherExceptionEnum|string Dishwasher exception.
