---Sustainable sourcing practices implemented at the hotel.
---@class gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcing
---@field ecoFriendlyToiletriesException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingEcoFriendlyToiletriesExceptionEnum|string Eco friendly toiletries exception.
---@field organicCageFreeEggsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingOrganicCageFreeEggsExceptionEnum|string Organic cage free eggs exception.
---@field responsiblePurchasingPolicyException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingResponsiblePurchasingPolicyExceptionEnum|string Responsible purchasing policy exception.
---@field responsiblePurchasingPolicy? boolean Responsible purchasing policy. The property has a responsible procurement policy in place. Responsible means integration of social, ethical, and/or environmental performance factors into the procurement process when selecting suppliers.
---@field organicFoodAndBeveragesException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingOrganicFoodAndBeveragesExceptionEnum|string Organic food and beverages exception.
---@field veganMealsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingVeganMealsExceptionEnum|string Vegan meals exception.
---@field locallySourcedFoodAndBeverages? boolean Locally sourced food and beverages. Property sources locally in order to lower the environmental footprint from reduced transportation and to stimulate the local economy. Products produced less than 62 miles from the establishment are normally considered as locally produced.
---@field vegetarianMealsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingVegetarianMealsExceptionEnum|string Vegetarian meals exception.
---@field veganMeals? boolean Vegan meals. The property provides vegan menu options for guests. Vegan food does not contain animal products or byproducts.
---@field ecoFriendlyToiletries? boolean Eco friendly toiletries. Soap, shampoo, lotion, and other toiletries provided for guests have a nationally or internationally recognized sustainability certification, such as USDA Organic, EU Organic, or cruelty-free.
---@field vegetarianMeals? boolean Vegetarian meals. The property provides vegetarian menu options for guests. Vegetarian food does not contain meat, poultry, fish, or seafood.
---@field locallySourcedFoodAndBeveragesException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingLocallySourcedFoodAndBeveragesExceptionEnum|string Locally sourced food and beverages exception.
---@field organicCageFreeEggs? boolean Organic cage free eggs. The property sources 100% certified organic and cage-free eggs (shell, liquid, and egg products). Cage-free means hens are able to walk, spread their wings and lay their eggs in nests).
---@field responsiblySourcesSeafood? boolean Responsibly sources seafood. The property does not source seafood from the Monterey Bay Aquarium Seafood Watch "avoid" list, and must sustainably source seafood listed as "good alternative," "eco-certified," and "best choice". The property has a policy outlining a commitment to source Marine Stewardship Council (MSC) and/or Aquaculture Stewardship Council (ASC) Chain of Custody certified seafood.
---@field organicFoodAndBeverages? boolean Organic food and beverages. At least 25% of food and beverages, by spend, are certified organic. Organic means products that are certified to one of the organic standard listed in the IFOAM family of standards. Qualifying certifications include USDA Organic and EU Organic, among others.
---@field responsiblySourcesSeafoodException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingResponsiblySourcesSeafoodExceptionEnum|string Responsibly sources seafood exception.

---@alias gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingEcoFriendlyToiletriesExceptionEnum "EXCEPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"UNDER_CONSTRUCTION"|"DEPENDENT_ON_SEASON"|"DEPENDENT_ON_DAY_OF_WEEK"

---@alias gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.SustainableSourcingLocallySourcedFoodAndBeveragesExceptionEnum "EXCEPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"UNDER_CONSTRUCTION"|"DEPENDENT_ON_SEASON"|"DEPENDENT_ON_DAY_OF_WEEK"

