---Waste reduction practices implemented at the hotel.
---@class gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReduction
---@field safelyDisposesLightbulbsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionSafelyDisposesLightbulbsExceptionEnum|string Safely disposes lightbulbs exception.
---@field safelyHandlesHazardousSubstances? boolean Safely handles hazardous substances. The property has a hazardous waste management program aligned wit GreenSeal and LEED requirements, and meets all regulatory requirements for hazardous waste disposal and recycling. Hazardous means substances that are classified as "hazardous" by an authoritative body (such as OSHA or DOT), are labeled with signal words such as "Danger," "Caution," "Warning," or are flammable, corrosive, or ignitable. Requirements include: - The property shall maintain records of the efforts it has made to replace the hazardous substances it uses with less hazardous alternatives. - An inventory of the hazardous materials stored on-site. - Products intended for cleaning, dishwashing, laundry, and pool maintenance shall be stored in clearly labeled containers. These containers shall be checked regularly for leaks, and replaced a necessary. - Spill containment devices shall be installed to collect spills, drips, or leaching of chemicals.
---@field compostableFoodContainersAndCutlery? boolean Compostable food containers and cutlery. 100% of food service containers and to-go cutlery are compostable, and reusable utensils are offered wherever possible. Compostable materials are capable of undergoing biological decomposition in a compost site, such that material is not visually distinguishable and breaks down into carbon dioxide, water, inorganic compounds, and biomass.
---@field safelyDisposesLightbulbs? boolean Safely disposes lightbulbs. The property safely stores and disposes lightbulbs.
---@field waterBottleFillingStations? boolean Water bottle filling stations. The property offers water stations throughout the building for guest use.
---@field donatesExcessFood? boolean Donates excess food. The property has a program and/or policy for diverting waste from landfill that may include efforts to donate for human consumption or divert food for animal feed.
---@field recyclingProgramException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionRecyclingProgramExceptionEnum|string Recycling program exception.
---@field soapDonationProgramException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionSoapDonationProgramExceptionEnum|string Soap donation program exception.
---@field noStyrofoamFoodContainers? boolean No styrofoam food containers. The property eliminates the use of Styrofoam in disposable food service items.
---@field recyclingProgram? boolean Recycling program. The property has a recycling program, aligned with LEED waste requirements, and a policy outlining efforts to send less than 50% of waste to landfill. The recycling program includes storage locations for recyclable materials, including mixed paper, corrugated cardboard, glass, plastics, and metals.
---@field compostsExcessFoodException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionCompostsExcessFoodExceptionEnum|string Composts excess food exception.
---@field toiletryDonationProgramException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionToiletryDonationProgramExceptionEnum|string Toiletry donation program exception.
---@field noStyrofoamFoodContainersException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionNoStyrofoamFoodContainersExceptionEnum|string No styrofoam food containers exception.
---@field noSingleUsePlasticWaterBottlesException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionNoSingleUsePlasticWaterBottlesExceptionEnum|string No single use plastic water bottles exception.
---@field soapDonationProgram? boolean Soap donation program. The property participates in a soap donation program such as Clean the World or something similar.
---@field waterBottleFillingStationsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionWaterBottleFillingStationsExceptionEnum|string Water bottle filling stations exception.
---@field compostableFoodContainersAndCutleryException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionCompostableFoodContainersAndCutleryExceptionEnum|string Compostable food containers and cutlery exception.
---@field foodWasteReductionProgramException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionFoodWasteReductionProgramExceptionEnum|string Food waste reduction program exception.
---@field safelyDisposesElectronicsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionSafelyDisposesElectronicsExceptionEnum|string Safely disposes electronics exception.
---@field compostsExcessFood? boolean Composts excess food. The property has a program and/or policy for diverting waste from landfill by composting food and yard waste, either through compost collection and off-site processing or on-site compost processing.
---@field refillableToiletryContainers? boolean Refillable toiletry containers. The property has replaced miniature individual containers with refillable amenity dispensers for shampoo, conditioner, soap, and lotion.
---@field donatesExcessFoodException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionDonatesExcessFoodExceptionEnum|string Donates excess food exception.
---@field safelyDisposesBatteriesException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionSafelyDisposesBatteriesExceptionEnum|string Safely disposes batteries exception.
---@field noSingleUsePlasticWaterBottles? boolean No single use plastic water bottles. The property bans single-use plastic water bottles.
---@field safelyDisposesElectronics? boolean Safely disposes electronics. The property has a reputable recycling program that keeps hazardous electronic parts and chemical compounds out of landfills, dumps and other unauthorized abandonment sites, and recycles/reuses applicable materials. (e.g. certified electronics recyclers).
---@field refillableToiletryContainersException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionRefillableToiletryContainersExceptionEnum|string Refillable toiletry containers exception.
---@field foodWasteReductionProgram? boolean Food waste reduction program. The property has established a food waste reduction and donation program, aiming to reduce food waste by half. These programs typically use tools such as the Hotel Kitchen Toolkit and others to track waste and measure progress.
---@field safelyDisposesBatteries? boolean Safely disposes batteries. The property safely stores and disposes batteries.
---@field safelyHandlesHazardousSubstancesException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionSafelyHandlesHazardousSubstancesExceptionEnum|string Safely handles hazardous substances exception.
---@field noSingleUsePlasticStraws? boolean No single use plastic straws. The property bans single-use plastic straws.
---@field noSingleUsePlasticStrawsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WasteReductionNoSingleUsePlasticStrawsExceptionEnum|string No single use plastic straws exception.
---@field toiletryDonationProgram? boolean Toiletry donation program. The property participates in a toiletry donation program such as Clean the World or something similar.

