---Water conservation practices implemented at the hotel.
---@class gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservation
---@field linenReuseProgram? boolean Linen reuse program. The property offers a linen reuse program.
---@field linenReuseProgramException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationLinenReuseProgramExceptionEnum|string Linen reuse program exception.
---@field waterSavingSinksException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationWaterSavingSinksExceptionEnum|string Water saving sinks exception.
---@field independentOrganizationAuditsWaterUseException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationIndependentOrganizationAuditsWaterUseExceptionEnum|string Independent organization audits water use exception.
---@field waterSavingShowers? boolean Water saving showers. All of the property's guest rooms have shower heads that use no more than 2.0 gallons per minute (gpm).
---@field waterSavingSinks? boolean Water saving sinks. All of the property's guest rooms have bathroom faucets that use a maximum of 1.5 gallons per minute (gpm), public restroom faucets do not exceed 0.5 gpm, and kitchen faucets (excluding faucets used exclusively for filling operations) do not exceed 2.2 gpm.
---@field waterSavingToiletsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationWaterSavingToiletsExceptionEnum|string Water saving toilets exception.
---@field waterSavingShowersException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationWaterSavingShowersExceptionEnum|string Water saving showers exception.
---@field towelReuseProgramException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationTowelReuseProgramExceptionEnum|string Towel reuse program exception.
---@field independentOrganizationAuditsWaterUse? boolean Independent organization audits water use. The property conducts a water conservation audit every 5 years, the results of which are either verified by a third-party and/or published in external communications. A water conservation audit is a detailed assessment of the facility, providing recommendations to existing operations and procedures to improve water efficiency, available incentives or rebates, and opportunities for improvements through renovations or upgrades. Examples of organizations who conduct credible third party audits include: Engie Impact, and local utility providers (they often provide energy and water audits).
---@field towelReuseProgram? boolean Towel reuse program. The property offers a towel reuse program.
---@field waterSavingToilets? boolean Water saving toilets. All of the property's toilets use 1.6 gallons per flush, or less.

---@alias gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationIndependentOrganizationAuditsWaterUseExceptionEnum "EXCEPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"UNDER_CONSTRUCTION"|"DEPENDENT_ON_SEASON"|"DEPENDENT_ON_DAY_OF_WEEK"

---@alias gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationLinenReuseProgramExceptionEnum "EXCEPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"UNDER_CONSTRUCTION"|"DEPENDENT_ON_SEASON"|"DEPENDENT_ON_DAY_OF_WEEK"

---@alias gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WaterConservationTowelReuseProgramExceptionEnum "EXCEPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"UNDER_CONSTRUCTION"|"DEPENDENT_ON_SEASON"|"DEPENDENT_ON_DAY_OF_WEEK"

