---Guest facilities at the property to promote or maintain health, beauty, and fitness.
---@class gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.Wellness
---@field salonException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessSalonExceptionEnum|string Salon exception.
---@field weightMachineException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessWeightMachineExceptionEnum|string Weight machine exception.
---@field freeWeightsException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessFreeWeightsExceptionEnum|string Free weights exception.
---@field salon? boolean Salon. A room at the hotel where professionals provide hair styling services such as shampooing, blow drying, hair dos, hair cutting and hair coloring. Also known as hairdresser or beauty salon.
---@field spaException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessSpaExceptionEnum|string Spa exception.
---@field ellipticalMachineException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessEllipticalMachineExceptionEnum|string Elliptical machine exception.
---@field freeFitnessCenter? boolean Free fitness center. Guests may use the fitness center for free.
---@field weightMachine? boolean Weight machine. Non-electronic fitness equipment designed for the user to target the exertion of different muscles. Usually incorporates a padded seat, a stack of flat weights and various bars and pulleys. May be designed for toning a specific part of the body or may involve different user-controlled settings, hardware and pulleys so as to provide an overall workout in one machine. Commonly found in a gym, fitness center, fitness room, or health club.
---@field sauna? boolean Sauna. A wood-paneled room heated to a high temperature where guests sit on built-in wood benches for the purpose of perspiring and relaxing their muscles. Can be dry or slightly wet heat. Not a steam room.
---@field fitnessCenter? boolean Fitness center. A room or building at the hotel containing equipment to promote physical activity, such as treadmills, elliptical machines, stationary bikes, weight machines, free weights, and/or stretching mats. Use of the fitness center can be free or for a fee. May or may not be staffed. May or may not offer instructor-led classes in various styles of physical conditioning. May or may not be open 24/7. May or may not include locker rooms and showers. Also known as health club, gym, fitness room, health center.
---@field treadmill? boolean Treadmill. An electric stationary fitness machine that simulates a moving path to promote walking or running within a range of user-controlled speeds and inclines. Also known as running machine. Commonly found in a gym, fitness room, health center, or health club.
---@field doctorOnCallException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessDoctorOnCallExceptionEnum|string Doctor on call exception.
---@field freeWeights? boolean Free weights. Individual handheld fitness equipment of varied weights used for upper body strength training or bodybuilding. Also known as barbells, dumbbells, or kettlebells. Often stored on a rack with the weights arranged from light to heavy. Commonly found in a gym, fitness room, health center, or health club.
---@field treadmillException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessTreadmillExceptionEnum|string Treadmill exception.
---@field fitnessCenterException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessFitnessCenterExceptionEnum|string Fitness center exception.
---@field massageException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessMassageExceptionEnum|string Massage exception.
---@field ellipticalMachine? boolean Elliptical machine. An electric, stationary fitness machine with pedals that simulates climbing, walking or running and provides a user-controlled range of speeds and tensions. May not have arm-controlled levers to work out the upper body as well. Commonly found in a gym, fitness room, health center, or health club.
---@field saunaException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessSaunaExceptionEnum|string Sauna exception.
---@field spa? boolean Spa. A designated area, room or building at the hotel offering health and beauty treatment through such means as steam baths, exercise equipment, and massage. May also offer facials, nail care, and hair care. Services are usually available by appointment and for an additional fee. Does not apply if hotel only offers a steam room; must offer other beauty and/or health treatments as well.
---@field doctorOnCall? boolean Doctor on call. The hotel has a contract with a medical professional who provides services to hotel guests should they fall ill during their stay. The doctor may or may not have an on-site office or be at the hotel at all times.
---@field freeFitnessCenterException? gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessFreeFitnessCenterExceptionEnum|string Free fitness center exception.
---@field massage? boolean Massage. A service provided by a trained massage therapist involving the physical manipulation of a guest's muscles in order to achieve relaxation or pain relief.

---@alias gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessDoctorOnCallExceptionEnum "EXCEPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"UNDER_CONSTRUCTION"|"DEPENDENT_ON_SEASON"|"DEPENDENT_ON_DAY_OF_WEEK"

---@alias gcp.mybusinesslodging_v1.WellnessEllipticalMachineExceptionEnum "EXCEPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"UNDER_CONSTRUCTION"|"DEPENDENT_ON_SEASON"|"DEPENDENT_ON_DAY_OF_WEEK"

